  {
    "pkheadingid": 751,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 581,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113521,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 581,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>All reported tumours arose in the parotid gland.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:21:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 752,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 582,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113522,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 582,
        "headingText": "<p >The tumour manifests as a painless, slowly growing parotid gland mass.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-10-18T14:47:38"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 753,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 583,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113523,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 583,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The patient age range is 8&ndash;49&nbsp;years {10335947; 12218219; 20702483; 22218263; 25960022; 31230813}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:21:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 754,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 584,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113524,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 584,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:21:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 755,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 585,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113525,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 585,
        "headingText": "<p>Keratocystoma is characterized by <em>RUNX2</em> rearrangements, mostly with <em>IRF2BP2</em>::<em>RUNX2</em> fusion {38084005}.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2023-12-19T12:51:57"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 762,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 592,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113526,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 592,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours range in size from 13&nbsp;to 40&nbsp;mm. The cut surface shows a multilocular cystic lesion filled with a keratin-like substance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:21:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 756,
    "bookid": 52,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 586,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 113527,
        "bookId": 52,
        "chapterId": 61,
        "headingId": 586,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour consists mainly of multiple cysts containing keratotic lamellae. Stratified squamous epithelium lines the cystic spaces and shows a parakeratotic or orthokeratotic surface, usually without a granular cell layer. The stratification of the epithelium is oriented regularly from the outer basal to the inner keratotic cell layers. Focally, the outer layer demonstrates bud-like protrusions, but no skin appendages are seen. In some areas, solid squamous cell islands with sharply defined margins are surrounded by collagenous stroma. The solid areas of squamous cell nests are localized partly within the parenchyma of the parotid gland adjacent to an excretory duct and should not be interpreted as invasive growth. Transformation from parotid ductal epithelium to neoplastic cells, through a squamous metaplasia&ndash;like process, may be present.</p>\r\n<p>Cells of the neoplastic squamous epithelium have uniform, bland nuclei and abundant eosinophilic cytoplasm. There is no oncocytic or mucous cell differentiation and no myxochondroid component. Foci of foreign body reaction against keratin and a dense lymphoid infiltration may be evident.</p>\r\n<h5>Immunohistochemistry</h5>\r\n<p>Immunostaining for S100, SMA, and calponin is negative.</p>\r\n<h5>Differential diagnosis</h5>\r\n<p>The differential diagnoses include primary and metastatic squamous cell carcinoma, mucoepidermoid carcinoma, metaplastic Warthin tumour, and necrotizing sialometaplasia. The absence of necrosis, invasion, and cytological atypia in keratocystoma weighs against malignancy.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2023-09-26T10:21:53"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 757,
    "bookid": 52,
